// Detection: Brute-force authentication
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1110 - Brute Force
// Data source: SecurityEvent (Windows Security Event Log via Azure Monitor Agent)
// Trigger event: 4625 (An account failed to log on)

SecurityEvent
| where EventID == 4625
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)
| summarize FailedAttempts = count(), 
            TargetAccounts = make_set(Account), 
            LatestAttempt = max(TimeGenerated)
            by IpAddress, Computer
| where FailedAttempts >= 5
| order by FailedAttempts desc

// Tuning notes:
// - Threshold (5 failures/hour) is a starting point; adjust based on baseline
//   noise observed in the lab environment before enabling as an analytics rule.
// - Consider excluding known service accounts / scheduled health-check sources
//   if they trigger false positives.
// - Pair with a follow-up query checking for a SUCCESSFUL logon (EventID 4624)
//   from the same IP shortly after the failed attempts, to prioritize
//   incidents where the brute force may have succeeded.
